  "id": "COMPOUND:29579 - PROTEIN:5849",
  "verbalization": "Ingenol-20-decanoate is implicated in the pathogenesis of A549 cells through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that this compound acts as a target for multiple molecules, which in turn target A549 cells. Specifically, Ingenol-20-decanoate is linked to Malme-3M, a cell line that is targeted by Oppsit-4(15)-Ene-1Beta,11-Diol and Notoamide B, both of which have a target relationship with A549. This indicates that the compound may exert its effects through a series of downstream pathways that ultimately lead to the activation or modulation of A549 cells. The presence of multiple targets, including those that are not directly linked to the compound, suggests a complex network of interactions that may involve various molecular mechanisms. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Ingenol-20-decanoate to influence A549 cells through a multi-tiered mechanism, possibly involving cellular signaling or metabolic processes.",
